dsh-perf-patch README · 1. The agent-mount `tools/change` storm：Suppress + synchronous flush is deliberate. Flushing via `queueMicrotask` starves the event
loop (listeners queue more microtasks than the loop drains) and was observed to freeze the UI;
that variant was removed and is not shipped.

dsh-perf-patch README · 3. dsh-ops asks a one-boolean question with a full prompt assembly：**Fix:** wrap `systemPrompt.assemble`. When — and only when — the call is one of those probes,
return a minimal assembly built from the same layers:

```js
{ sections: [{ name: 'tools:ptc-only', text }], contexts: [], tools: [] }
```
